course: dictionary
lesson: 13181
title: Frequency: how often
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Frequency means how often something happens. «The buses run with a high frequency: one comes every five minutes.» Five minutes between buses is a short gap, so a high frequency means something happens many times in a short time.
explain: In maths, frequency counts how many times a value appears in a set of data. In a tally chart, the value with the highest frequency is the one you see most. In science, frequency counts how many waves pass a point each second, and it is measured in hertz (Hz).
explain: Check the meaning by swapping your idea into the sentence. «The frequency of the buses is every five minutes» makes sense if frequency means how often. Look for clue words in the context: «how often», «how many times» and «each second» all point to frequency.
fact: Frequency is a noun. Its plural is frequencies.
fact: «Frequency» means how often something happens.
fact: In maths, the frequency of a value is the number of times it appears in the data. The highest frequency is the mode.
fact: In science, frequency is how many waves pass a point each second, measured in hertz (Hz).
fact: High-frequency sounds are high-pitched, like a whistle.
exercise: «The buses have a high frequency: one arrives every five minutes.» What does frequency mean here? | How long the journey takes | *How often the buses come | The colour of the buses | How many seats there are on a bus
exercise: Ella counts the colours in her bag. Red appears 4 times and blue appears 2 times. What is the frequency of red? | 6 | *4 | 2 | 42
exercise: «The mode is the value with the highest frequency.» Which word means how often a value appears? | *frequency | highest | mode | value
test: In science, frequency is measured in which unit? | *Hertz (Hz) | Kilograms | Metres | Litres
test: Which sound has a high frequency? | *High-pitched, like a whistle | Very quiet, like a whisper | A sound that never changes at all | Low and deep, like thunder
exam: Jayden says frequency means how big something is. Is he right? | Yes, it means how big something is | *No, frequency means how often something happens | Yes, it means the colour of something | It means the same as weight
